#   mnx test-status / mnx test-cancel / mnx test-errors
#   mnx m21-identity / mnx m21-enroll / mnx m21-helper status / mnx btrfs-baseline status
#   mnx restic policy / status / maintenance-recover / enroll / qualify / verify / self-test
#   mnx baseline repeatability / mnx baseline capture pre-refactor --pin
#   mnx port review SOURCE
#   mnx doctor / mnx brief / mnx evidence verify
#   mnx cloudtainer policy / status / candidate / pack / self-test
#   mnx office resume / mnx office agenda expose the stage-bound source capsule plus finalized runtime overlay
#   mnx eject plan / mnx eject transforms / mnx eject preview / mnx eject self-test / mnx eject verify
#   mnx capsule policy / mnx capsule inspect / mnx capsule verify / mnx capsule self-test
#   mnx substrate status / contract / reconstruction / backup-soak / self-test
#   mnx incident journal status / verify / evidence; anchor --switch-owned is reserved for accepted switch continuation
#   monsterdesk doctor / start [--show] / demo / observe / mcp / mcp-config / self-test
#   mnx upgrade policy / check / build / status / evidence
# Upgrade build output identity comes only from a dedicated stdout evidence file; diagnostic stderr is
# independently retained and may contain arbitrary binary/control bytes without influencing path selection.
#   mnx desktop policy / audit / self-test
#   mnx-configuration-as-bash test
#   mnxcrypt create / open / status / unmount / fsck / info / gui / doctor / policy / self-test
#   presslog arm / stop / disarm / pause / resume / toggle / status / doctor / verify / policy / self-test
#   monsterkey status / toggle / policy / self-test
# Bare `mnx` is the read-only identity-first officer wake action. The two routine operator mutation commands are
# `mnx test` and `mnx switch`; neither depends on the downloaded file retaining an executable bit.
# Any routine continuation whose trigger is knowable from accepted source and switch state belongs inside `mnx switch`;
# the operator is not expected to infer or remember a third command. Candidate-declared post-acceptance actions run only
# after exact promotion, behavior adoption, atomic office commit, strict post-commit verification, and lock release.
# One-shot diagnostics and rehearsals leave the successor plan once their evidence question is answered; their explicit
# commands and manifested evidence remain available without taxing every later configuration transaction.
# A currently installed older harness accepts a newer source when its one MNX_DOCUMENT_SCHEMA declaration and
# final nonblank sentinel agree; detailed schema rules remain the candidate-owned source lexer's responsibility.
# Activation repairs /etc/nixos/configuration.nix to mode 0755, after which the direct shebang entry point also works:
#   sudo /etc/nixos/configuration.nix test
# Before the generation that provides `mnx` is active, use the already-installed extractor:
#   sudo env MNX_CONFIG=/etc/nixos/configuration.nix mnx-configuration-as-bash test
# The shebang self-extracts and executes the commented Section-99 Bash payload.
# The former hand-toggled heredoc scaffold was removed; Section 99 is the only supported source-as-Bash path.

