#@MNX-FLOW id=amnesia-capsule-replacement kind=governance title="Editing ChatGPT turn close to one stage-bound source capsule plus finalized runtime overlay" source="current operator request, exact candidate source, accepted predecessor office, and finalized switch/continuation evidence" destination="one replacement #@MNX-AMNESIA block plus bounded mnx office resume and mnx brief outputs" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' programs="mnx-office,mnx,mnx-source-lexer" lock=none state="exact capsule bytes inside configuration.nix; runtime overlay derived from accepted switch report and optional /var/lib/monsternix/post-acceptance receipt" notes="The editing ChatGPT injects the capsule before delivering the complete candidate. Test rejects stale/duplicate/oversize capsules. Switch never rewrites source; finalized evidence may change the effective next objective without changing accepted history."
#@MNX-LAW id=amnesia-capsule-is-single-and-stage-bound severity=hard title="The amnesia capsule is one exact replacement block" statement="Schema-47+ candidates contain exactly one bounded public capsule whose stage and predecessor identity match the office agenda; every new candidate replaces it rather than appending another diary." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="exact begin/end grammar, required ordered fields, stage/predecessor equality, byte/field ceilings, obvious-secret rejection, exact capsule SHA-256, candidate agenda validation, and adversarial self-test"
#@MNX-LAW id=amnesia-capsule-is-inherited-intent severity=hard title="The capsule never impersonates a current request" statement="The capsule is compressed inherited intent authored into a candidate; the live operator request outranks it and no machine/model text can self-authorize work." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="fixed AUTHORITY field, office/brief epistemic labels, source policy text, and source lexer landmarks"
#@MNX-LAW id=finalized-runtime-overlay-selects-effective-next severity=hard title="Finalized evidence may override declared next work" statement="Office resume and brief print both the source-declared objective and the effective objective derived from the exact finalized switch result and source-bound continuation receipt; blockers and contract violations cannot be hidden by a stale agenda." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="exact switch-report parsing, contained receipt verification, core/final result separation, declared/effective fields, and brief priority ordering"
#@MNX-LAW id=accepted-source-is-never-rewritten-for-handoff severity=hard title="Runtime handoff never mutates accepted source" statement="The editing ChatGPT injects the capsule before test; acceptance records runtime overlay separately. No post-switch tool edits configuration.nix to update prose." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="exact source/active/default hashes, source_mutated_during_switch=no, office record source identity, and separate post-acceptance receipt"
#@MNX-LAW id=source-history-is-bounded-and-distilled severity=hard title="The source is not an infinite session transcript" statement="Stable lessons graduate into laws and subsystem summaries, one current capsule carries compressed state, and exact older detail remains in immutable office/test/switch evidence instead of endlessly expanding Sections 01-09." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="source-history policy marker, single capsule, bounded capsule bytes, stage-local closed_issue, and future recent-window compaction objective"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-is-derived-command-center severity=hard title="Cloudtainer is a portable command center, not another authority" statement="mnx cloudtainer may package exact source, office, finalized runtime evidence, maps, and portable read-only tools for a ChatGPT office-holder, but neither packet prose nor the cloud container gains mutation authority over monster-16." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' enforcement="explicit authority labels, exact source hash, no payload execution, no network, standard-library portable helper, source-owned two-command acceptance, and candidate/runtime self-tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-packets-are-contained-and-secret-minimized severity=hard title="Cloudtainer packets are exact, contained, and narrowly scoped" statement="A packet contains the exact public monolith and selected office/evidence views but never reads private keys, runtime credentials, arbitrary home files, or paths outside its declared bundle; every regular payload is bound by a self-excluding relative SHA-256 manifest." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-bundle-manifest"' enforcement="fixed packet inventory, canonical manifest verifier, no symlink payloads, explicit output root, root:logbook metadata, adversarial fixture, and no implicit persistent write"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-refresh-is-switch-owned severity=hard title="Accepted switches refresh the ChatGPT command center automatically" statement="When a candidate declares cloudtainer-pack, mnx switch commits and seals the exact candidate first, releases transaction locks, then emits one source-bound packet so the operator never has to infer a third routine command." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx"' enforcement="fixed post-acceptance allowlist, cloudtainer-pack action, source/runtime nonmutation proof, manifested packet, source-bound continuation receipt, and switch self-tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-portable-code-is-atlas-anchored severity=hard title="Portable cloudtainer code obeys the monolith atlas" statement="Every class and function declaration carried inside the portable cloudtainer helper has one immediately preceding truthful PART anchor in the authoritative monolith, and the cloudtainer self-test rejects missing or stale anchors before candidate acceptance." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="portable-source class/function scan, exact marker adjacency and kind matching, public cloudtainer self-test output contract, source-lexer landmark, activation atlas, and adversarial regression"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-turn-close-is-render-only severity=hard title="Turn close renders the next handoff but never edits accepted source" statement="mnx cloudtainer turn-close deterministically renders the next candidate capsule and bounded history ledger from exact accepted source identity; it performs no live-source replacement and grants no mutation authority." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="source-bound next-stage/predecessor derivation, bounded field grammar, exact history rollover, no write path, packet fixture, and public self-test"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-history-ledger-is-exact-and-bounded severity=hard title="Recent accepted history is one exact eight-record ledger" statement="The source contains one ascending ledger whose last entry equals the candidate predecessor; every next candidate rolls in the accepted current source and drops only the oldest entry while immutable office evidence retains full history." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="single begin/end grammar, exactly eight records, stage/hash/token validation, predecessor equality, turn-close rollover, packet inclusion, and adversarial self-test"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-candidate-workspace-is-contained severity=hard title="Candidate workspaces are disposable and cannot become host authority" statement="A cloudtainer workspace may contain one exact accepted source and one complete editable candidate, but it may write only beneath an explicit nonpacket, nonprotected workspace/proposal root and never modifies live source, profiles, packet contents, or host state." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="path containment and symlink refusal, protected-root denylist, exact accepted-source hash, read-only baseline copy, explicit output arguments, standard-library helper, adversarial workspace self-test, and no source execution/network"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-candidate-review-is-advisory severity=hard title="Static cloudtainer review is evidence rather than acceptance" statement="Candidate check, definition-body hash delta, risk buckets, and unified diff help the office-holder inspect a proposal but cannot prove Nix evaluation, runtime behavior, or safety and never authorize activation." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="review authority labels, host-validation-required fields, explicit unknowns, no Nix invocation, and ordinary exact candidate test/switch contract"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-handoff-injection-is-workspace-only severity=hard title="Controlled handoff replacement never edits accepted source" statement="Capsule, history, and combined turn-close injection are atomic replacements against the disposable candidate only, require exact stage/predecessor rollover and reject malformed or secret-like material; packet and live source remain untouched." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="single marker pairs, candidate workspace containment, stable-read identity, field/order/size grammar, history rollover check, atomic replace, before/after source hashes, and injection self-test"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-proposals-carry-complete-source severity=hard title="A proposal contains the complete candidate and never substitutes a diff" statement="Cloudtainer packaging requires a structurally passing complete candidate and carries exact accepted and proposed source bytes, review, check, diff, capsule, history, agenda, portable verifier, and self-excluding manifest in a deterministic archive; host acceptance is still required." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-bundle-manifest"' enforcement="candidate check gate, complete-source inventory, regular-file relative manifest, proposal verifier, deterministic metadata, diff-is-evidence marker, and proposal self-test"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-workspace-static-files-are-manifested severity=hard title="Candidate workspace static provenance is independently bound" statement="Every static workspace file is recorded in WORKSPACE-SHA256SUMS and verified on every load; editable candidate.nix and the manifest itself are deliberately excluded so proposal editing remains possible without weakening accepted-source provenance." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="canonical relative regular-file manifest, exact inventory equality, digest verification before candidate actions, tamper self-test, and workspace-manifest marker required by source and runtime audits"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-policy-is-self-consistent severity=hard title="Cloudtainer policy has one mechanically verified JSON shape" statement="The host policy command, candidate-workspace policy, packet metadata, portable self-test, and runtime audit agree on schema, authority, network and mutation bounds, and host-validation requirements; no consumer may silently look in a different JSON branch." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="canonical JSON roundtrip, review-plus-proposal host-validation flags, public policy command contract, aggregate self-test marker, source landmark, and candidate postflight"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-closed-trees-have-exact-inventory severity=hard title="Verified cloudtainer objects are exact closed trees" statement="Packet, proposal, and workspace verification binds every permitted file and directory and rejects every unmanifested entry, link, special file, missing entry, duplicate, alias, or self-reference." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="canonical TREE-MANIFEST.json plus SHA256SUMS, exact inventory equality, lstat type checks, byte counts, stable reads, adversarial extras and links, and optimized-mode self-tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-metadata-is-recomputed-from-carried-bytes severity=hard title="Carried metadata is checked against carried source" statement="Source, candidate, capsule, history, agenda, helper, diff, review, packet, and proposal identity fields are recomputed from the bytes in the verified object; regenerating an unsigned manifest cannot bless false metadata." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="independent source parsing and digest recomputation, mutual metadata cross-checks, falsified-candidate-sha regression, and explicit refusal rather than trust in JSON assertions"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-archives-are-verified-before-materialization severity=hard title="Archives are member-checked before extraction" statement="A cloudtainer archive is walked and bounded before any member is written; only one canonical root and manifest-agreeing regular files/directories are eligible for private materialization." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="duplicate/alias/absolute/traversal/link/device/FIFO/PAX/type/count/size rejection, decompressed bounds, private materialization, closed-tree re-verification, and malicious-member tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-proof-does-not-depend-on-python-assert severity=hard title="Optimization cannot erase acceptance proof" statement="No packet, proposal, workspace, archive, or publication acceptance witness depends on Python assert because optimized Python removes assertions." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="zero executable asserts in portable and host planner acceptance paths, explicit require/refusal branches, normal plus python -O test suites, and producer/runtime receipts"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-content-and-publication-identities-are-separate severity=hard title="Semantic content identity is independent of publication naming" statement="The deterministic identity of meaningful packet/proposal content excludes timestamped destinations and publication receipts; output-directory renaming cannot change the deterministic archive bytes." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor"' enforcement="constant archive roots, normalized carried paths, canonical metadata, two-output-name byte comparison, semantic_content_sha256, and separate PUBLICATION.json"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-publication-is-atomic-and-restorable severity=hard title="Interrupted publication preserves the previous completed object" statement="Cloudtainer publication builds and verifies privately, fsyncs content, atomically renames completed packet and archive, and retains prior completed objects until the replacements pass post-publication verification." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="temporary packet/archive, prepublication verification, parent fsync, backup renames, injected mid-publication failure, exact prior-object restoration, and final published-object verification"
#@MNX-LAW id=cloudtainer-network-claim-is-invocation-scoped severity=hard title="A network-free verifier invocation is not an ambient sandbox claim" statement="network_api_or_tool_invoked=false reports only that the named verification path invoked no network API or tool; it never claims the surrounding cloud container lacked network reachability." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="separate network_api_or_tool_invoked and ambient_network_sandbox_proved fields, policy prose, packet receipts, portable doctor, and JSON contract tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=office-holder-is-first-class-user severity=hard title="An amnesiac officer gets an obvious identity-first wake path" statement="Bare host mnx and bare packet bin/mnx-cloudtainer are the one obvious read-only wake actions; each classifies exact identity before advice, states authority, separates current request from inherited intent and evidence, names effective next work and uncertainty, prints the exact two-command acceptance surface on one screen, and then progressively discloses deeper machinery." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="officer-wake schema, default-command dispatch, bounded compact renderer, full/JSON disclosure, packet closed-tree verification before OFFICER-BRIEF output, host and portable cold-start fixtures, tamper refusal, source/runtime overlay reconciliation, and no mutation authority"

#@MNX-LAW id=source-landmarks-name-source-syntax severity=hard title="Source landmarks preserve literal source spelling" statement="A validator searching configuration.nix must match the literal source expression, including `${pkgs...}` syntax; Nix-rendered store paths are verified separately as generated or closure evidence and may never replace source-syntax landmarks." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-program-audit",system.activationScripts.mnx-rendered-program-and-monolith-gate' enforcement="escaped Nix interpolation in generated lexer literals, runtime no-store-path assertion, package checkPhase grep, source-parser marker, and predecessor regression"
#@MNX-FLOW id=refactor-frontier kind=governance title="Exact source atlas to low-coupling frontier, impact plans, and disposable workspaces" source="truthful CHUNK/DEF/PART atlas plus explicit FLOW/LAW relationships" destination="bounded plans and root-owned derived workspaces under /var/lib/logbook/support/refactor-workspaces" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-atlas",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-relations",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' programs="mnx-refactor,mnx-atlas,mnx-relations,mnx-office" lock=none state="/var/lib/logbook/support/refactor-workspaces" notes="Risk scores are heuristic navigation, never permission; configuration.nix remains authoritative and plain mnx test is always the first validation command."
#@MNX-FLOW id=generic-cross-port-review kind=governance title="Foreign Monsternix source to bounded cross-port classification" source="operator-supplied readable source treated only as exact bytes and UTF-8 text" destination="portable-law, portable-mechanism, adapter-pattern, machine-binding, conflict, and unknown review" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' programs="mnx-refactor,mnx" lock=none state=none notes="The reviewer caps source size, verifies a stable read, executes and evaluates nothing from the foreign source, writes no configuration, and emits advisory evidence rather than transfer authority."
#@MNX-FLOW id=plain-nixos-ejection-groundwork kind=portability title="Owned monolith to exact nonpublishing plain-NixOS transformation inventory" source="exact source bytes, truthful DEF ranges, explicit MNX-EJECT ownership markers, and accepted definition-body hashes" destination="keep/remove/transform inventory with total contract coverage and explicit behavior gaps" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-eject",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' programs="mnx-eject,mnx" lock=none state=none notes="The planner executes no source, mutates no configuration, binds every mixed definition to one accepted body hash, and retains publication as a hard refusal."
#@MNX-FLOW id=plain-nixos-ejection-transform-preview kind=portability title="Exact mixed-definition contracts to a nonpersistent ordinary-module preview" source="38 body-hash-bound transformation contracts plus three exact residual rewrites" destination="Nix-parsed control-plane-language-free preview and a twenty-item behavior-gap ledger" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-eject",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' programs="mnx-eject,mnx" lock=none state=none notes="Preview bytes exist only in a private temporary directory or explicit stdout, never become source or accepted behavior, and cannot be published before replacement/disposition and behavior witnesses are reviewed."
#@MNX-FLOW id=capsule-identity-inspection kind=portability title="Carried bytes to bounded nonexecuting capsule identity evidence" source="operator-selected readable regular file capped at 16 MiB" destination="stable path/size/digest/media/mode evidence or exact expected-byte verification" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' programs="mnx-refactor,mnx" lock=none state=none notes="Inspection follows a stable bounded read, discloses symlinks, executes no payload, uses no network, writes no persistent state, and refuses run until a later reviewed sandbox/receipt contract exists."
#@MNX-FLOW id=substrate-continuity-contract kind=portability title="Current NixOS adapter to substrate-independent Monsternix contract inventory" source="exact source identity plus current runtime adapter facts" destination="portable protocol/evidence contracts, explicit non-portability limits, and migration-witness requirements" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' programs="mnx-refactor,mnx,mnx-office" lock=none state=none notes="The status and contract surfaces are read-only and network-free; they name NixOS as current and replaceable without claiming that the present monolith already executes on another substrate."
#@MNX-FLOW id=foundation-brief-handoff kind=governance title="Accepted office plus fresh bounded facts to one identity-first wake screen" source="editable/active/default source identities, accepted office record, current metrics, exposure ledger, freshness state, transaction state, and failed units" destination="bare mnx compact wake, mnx brief --full/JSON, and optional manifested support bundle" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-bundle-manifest"' programs="mnx,mnx-office,mnx-exposure,mnx-bundle-manifest" lock=none state="optional /var/lib/logbook/support/mnx-brief-* bundle" notes="Identity is classified before advice; every conclusion keeps its epistemic kind; default output is bounded, read-only, and network-free; full and JSON views are progressive disclosure."
