#@MNX-LAW id=maintained-font-coverage-over-dead-archives severity=hard title="Broad font coverage must not depend on dead archival sources" statement="The machine favors maintained Noto, CJK, emoji, Unicode, symbol, metric-compatible, and legacy compatibility families; repeated dead-mirror packages are removed rather than locally impersonated or retried forever." defs='fonts,environment.systemPackages,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="exact source markers, no active textfonts token in fonts or systemPackages, runtime Fontconfig audit, immutable upgrade rebuild evidence, and ordinary behavior-reviewed test/switch acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=gtk-defaults-are-system-readable-user-overridable severity=hard title="GTK defaults are declarative without becoming a forced theme prison" statement="GTK3 and GTK4 receive readable XDG defaults, dconf schemas, maintained icon/theme data, and the GTK portal; global GTK_THEME and ADW_DISABLE_PORTAL overrides remain absent so operator home settings can take precedence." defs='environment.etc."xdg/gtk-3.0/settings.ini".text,environment.etc."xdg/gtk-4.0/settings.ini".text,programs.dconf.enable,xdg.portal,environment.systemPackages,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx"' enforcement="source lexer policy checks, public mnx desktop self-test/policy/audit, generated-program checkPhase, and post-activation config audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=desktop-schema-audit-is-source-owned severity=hard title="Desktop schema proof uses an exact source-owned package path" statement="A root shell or system profile may omit package-specific GSettings search paths even when the package is installed; the desktop audit therefore verifies org.gnome.desktop.interface through the exact gsettings-desktop-schemas store output selected by the candidate, not ambient session discovery." defs='environment.systemPackages,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="source marker, exact package interpolation, compiled-schema check in generated-program checkPhase, runtime schema directory/count evidence, JSON contract, and candidate postflight"
#@MNX-LAW id=routine-post-acceptance-work-is-switch-owned severity=hard title="Knowable post-acceptance triggers are not operator homework" statement="When accepted source and switch state fully determine a safe routine continuation, the candidate declares it and mnx switch runs it after exact promotion, behavior adoption, atomic office commit, strict seal, and lock release; the operator is not expected to infer or remember another command." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' enforcement="single source marker, action allowlist, post-commit seal, released transaction/storage locks, exact-source receipt, switch transcript fields, source lexer, and switch self-test"
#@MNX-LAW id=post-acceptance-blockers-do-not-rewrite-acceptance severity=hard title="A continuation blocker is next-stage evidence, not a failed accepted switch" statement="Once exact promotion, behavior adoption, office commit, and strict post-commit seal succeed, a bounded continuation may report pass, deferred, or blocker, but it may not roll back or mutate the accepted profile, behavior baseline, office record, source, channel, or old-storage." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-upgrade"' enforcement="continuation starts only after core commit and lock release, action-specific no-mutation contracts, immutable per-source receipt, separate result fields, PASS_WITH_POST_ACCEPTANCE_* switch status, and no fail_core path after continuation begins"
#@MNX-LAW id=post-acceptance-is-outside-core-rollback-boundary severity=hard title="Sealed acceptance is not undone by continuation control flow" statement="Once the exact promoted closure, reviewed behavior baseline, and office record pass the post-commit seal, transaction locks are released and later continuation deferral, blocker, interruption, or contract failure cannot invoke the core switch rollback path; any protected-state mismatch is a hard visible incident against the accepted state." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' enforcement="phase-aware signal handling, no fail_core call after lock release, core_acceptance_result transcript field, protected-state mutation proof, and source lexer landmarks"
#@MNX-FLOW id=switch-core-final-result kind=transaction title="Core acceptance to final switch result" source="exact tested closure, reviewed behavior baseline, committed office record, and explicit pre-seal core intent" destination="one final switch result that preserves core acceptance while recording post-acceptance pass, blocker, deferral, interruption, or contract incident" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx"' programs="mnx-switch,mnx-office,mnx" state="open switch transcript, office record, final transcript epilogue" notes="The office binds the core PASS/PASS_ALREADY_ACTIVE_DEFAULT result. The final mnx_switch_result may carry a validated post-acceptance suffix without invalidating accepted truth."
#@MNX-LAW id=office-binds-core-switch-result severity=hard title="The office binds core acceptance, not continuation outcome" statement="The switch-committed office record binds only PASS or PASS_ALREADY_ACTIVE_DEFAULT for the exact promoted closure; the one final transaction result may add a validated post-acceptance blocker, deferral, or interruption suffix, or report a post-acceptance contract incident, without rewriting core acceptance." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="switch result schema 2, core/final relationship validator, status-specific suffix allowlist, canonical switch evidence digest, and office self-test"
#@MNX-LAW id=open-switch-report-seal-is-explicit severity=hard title="Post-commit sealing may inspect an open transcript only through an explicit state" statement="After office commit but before continuation determines the final switch result, office and doctor verification may accept the open report only when the switch declares its intended core result, the internal post-commit-seal environment is present, and every ordinary source, closure, test, baseline, office, and old-storage invariant passes." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-upgrade"' enforcement="hidden allow-incomplete flag, MNX_OFFICE_POST_COMMIT_SEAL gate, committed-pending-final-seal state, exact intended-result marker, doctor JSON assertion, and final strict validation"
#@MNX-LAW id=switch-maintenance-wait-is-bounded severity=hard title="A routine maintenance race is waited out before returning operator work" statement="Before taking transaction locks, mnx switch waits a bounded interval for known heavy maintenance while continuously requiring the editable source and tested running closure to remain exact; only timeout or changed identity returns a visible deferral or failure." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="two-hour default bound, sixty-second progress, fifteen-second polling, source/tested-closure identity checks, pre-lock wait, post-lock race check, and transcript fields"
#@MNX-LAW id=operator-lane-distinguishes-exclusion-from-contention severity=hard title="Background maintenance does not turn h0p3 into a polling loop" statement="mnx test and mnx switch queue for the shared mutation lock; scheduled lock users never queue behind or overtake the operator. Only the idempotent monthly rsync mirror may be manager-stopped after exact unit/PID/invocation/hardening proof, lock release, private-namespace teardown, and host read-only verification; backup, scrub, GC, and dedupe work remains nonpreemptible." defs='services.fstrim,services.btrfs.autoScrub,systemd.services.btrbk-main,systemd.services.btrbk-archive-to-new-storage,systemd.services.rsync-m16-new-to-old,systemd.services.m21-btrfs-pull-backup,systemd.services.m16-backup-m21,systemd.services.m16-restic-maintenance,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-behavior-manifest",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor"' enforcement="lock-first signal-cancellable source/running/default/health-stable wait, one nonblocking background lock attempt, rsync-only manager stop with bounded identity evidence, SuccessExitStatus 75 and read-only restoration trap, intentional-failure filtering then exact reset, root-scrub exclusion, new-storage-scrub/fstrim advisories, generated-program tests, and transcript fields"
#@MNX-LAW id=operator-preemption-is-rsync-only-and-retryable severity=hard title="Interactive transactions may preempt only the restartable browseable mirror" statement="When rsync-m16-new-to-old already owns the shared storage lock, mnx test or mnx switch may request one asynchronous manager stop because the mirror is idempotent, has no success advancement on interruption, and restores its private old-storage view read-only. No other heavy-storage unit is preemptible." defs='systemd.services.rsync-m16-new-to-old,systemd.timers.rsync-m16-new-to-old,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",fileSystems."/mnt/m16-old-storage"' enforcement="single literal unit allowlist, loaded/active/MainPID/InvocationID/PrivateMounts/KillMode/Restart checks, systemctl --no-block stop, shared-lock release, deactivating-state wait, exact expected post-stop Result/ExecMainCode/ExecMainStatus, host findmnt ro proof, reset-failed limited to the named unit, SuccessExitStatus 75, noncritical retryable metric reason, no last-success write, source/runtime audits, and adversarial static gates"
#@MNX-LAW id=single-authoritative-monolith severity=hard title="configuration.nix is the only authoritative machine source" statement="Derived chunks, definitions, parts, relationship cards, bundles, and admin copies never become imports or co-equal source trees." defs='imports,system.copySystemConfiguration' enforcement="empty imports, exact closure-embedded source hash, split/join roundtrip, and office constitution"
#@MNX-LAW id=no-import-tree severity=hard title="No module/import tree" statement="The active configuration keeps imports = [ ]; and remains one complete copy/pasteable file." defs='imports' enforcement="evaluation assertion by source lexer and atlas policy"
#@MNX-LAW id=scoped-nix-bindings-are-explicit-and-liftable severity=hard title="Modern Nix may compress facts but never hide authority" statement="Inside the one complete source, let/in, inherit, functions, recursive attribute sets, assertions, lib combinators, option types, and submodules are permitted when they single-source machine facts or validate a visible interface; imports remain empty, dynamic source discovery is forbidden, and abstractions may not conceal privileged bodies, state mutation, trust, secrets, rollback, or operator-owned material." defs='imports,environment.etc."monsternix/nix-language.json".text,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="machine-readable language contract plus typed semantic kernel built by real top-level let/function/inherit and lib.evalModules expressions, active-token evidence, exact Nix parse, immutable NixOS /etc symlink-chain validation to bounded root-owned nonwritable Nix-store files, one-file atlas, plain-ejection compatibility, and behavior-reviewed acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=generated-programs-stay-embedded severity=hard title="Generated programs remain visibly embedded" statement="Every machine-authored Monsternix program is generated from a complete source block in configuration.nix; no hidden hand-maintained script tree is introduced." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-program-audit"' enforcement="writeTextFile checkPhase plus rendered-source audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=test-before-switch severity=hard title="Every candidate is tested before permanent promotion" statement="mnx switch accepts only secure completed evidence for the exact current source hash." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="test transcript and frozen candidate evidence"
#@MNX-LAW id=exact-tested-closure-promotion severity=hard title="Switch promotes the exact tested closure" statement="mnx switch sets the system profile to the exact closure activated by mnx test and does not rebuild or reevaluate channels." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",system.copySystemConfiguration' enforcement="closure hash checks, profile set, switch-to-configuration, and rollback"
#@MNX-LAW id=office-acceptance-is-switch-committed severity=hard title="The live office advances only after exact permanent acceptance" statement="The source owns the agenda, but current.json is atomically replaced only after exact tested closure activation, postflight, and behavior-contract acceptance; rollback restores the predecessor pointer." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="root-owned schema-1 record, canonical finalization-stable semantic evidence digest with narrow legacy transition support, atomic record-plus-symlink commit, bounded resume verification, and switch recovery"
#@MNX-LAW id=office-evidence-survives-logbook-retention severity=hard title="Accepted office evidence survives ordinary support pruning" statement="Every test and switch transcript referenced by an office acceptance record remains available for later verification even after ordinary 90-day support retention." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",systemd.services.mnx-logbook-prune' enforcement="strict JSON extraction of referenced reports and exact-path exclusion from support deletion"
#@MNX-LAW id=upgrade-target-is-immutable severity=hard title="Upgrade builds use one pinned immutable supported-series source" statement="The source-owned upgrade build accepts only the declared NixOS series, release URL, Git revision, and official flat archive SHA-256; it verifies that archive before unpacking the same store object locally, while a moving feed and the resulting unpacked NAR identity are observations rather than implicit authority." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-upgrade",system.autoUpgrade.enable' enforcement="source constants, HTTPS feed/release checks, exact revision, expected flat-file hash, local-file unpack, generated-program self-tests, and manifested raw plus unpacked identities"
#@MNX-LAW id=upgrade-build-never-activates severity=hard title="Upgrade check and build never activate, promote, or reboot" statement="The upgrade rehearsal may resolve network metadata, write the Nix store, and create bounded support evidence, but under h0p3's standing no-reboot instruction it may not call switch-to-configuration, mutate the system profile, mutate the root channel profile or subscription, change stateVersion, reboot, or write old-storage; a successful build is evidence only." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-upgrade",system.autoUpgrade.enable,boot.initrd.systemd.enable,services.dbus.implementation,programs.fuse.enable' enforcement="dedicated nonactivating build command, classic-D-Bus and legacy-initrd compatibility gates, explicit FUSE enablement, before/after identity proof, explicit status-69 test/switch refusals, no timer, shared storage lock, and source/runtime audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=upgrade-evidence-binds-source-release-and-closure severity=hard title="Upgrade evidence binds exact source, release, and closure" statement="A successful upgrade build is meaningful only when its manifested bundle binds the accepted configuration bytes, pinned release revision and flat archive hash, resulting unpacked Nixpkgs identity, compatibility projection, staged system closure, closure difference, and no-mutation postflight." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-upgrade",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-bundle-manifest"' enforcement="root-owned candidate freeze, exact embedded-source hash, canonical evidence manifest, independent status verification, and source/channel/profile/closure postflight comparison"
#@MNX-LAW id=upgrade-build-output-path-is-stdout-only severity=hard title="Upgrade closure identity is parsed only from dedicated stdout" statement="The successful nix-build output path is authority only when one dedicated stdout evidence file contains exactly one canonical NixOS store path; arbitrary stderr diagnostics, progress text, control bytes, and binary-looking logs never participate in path selection." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-upgrade",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="separate stdout/stderr files, exact single-line parser, canonical store-path grammar, binary-safe diagnostic classification, manifested stdout witness, adversarial self-test, and explicit operator-invoked rebuild"
#@MNX-LAW id=unattended-upgrades-never-switch severity=hard title="Unattended upgrades never mutate running or boot-default closure identity" statement="No timer may invoke a raw nixos-rebuild switch or boot operation outside the exact mnx test and mnx switch acceptance transaction." defs='system.autoUpgrade.enable,assertions,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="system.autoUpgrade disabled, evaluation assertion, exact closure-bound office record, source-pinned one-time drift transition, and self-describing postflight diagnostics"
#@MNX-LAW id=refactor-views-are-derived severity=hard title="Refactor plans and workspaces never become source authority" statement="Frontier rankings, impact reports, plan JSON, exact definition slices, and disposable workspaces are derived evidence only; they are never imported, joined automatically, or treated as a co-equal machine definition." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-atlas",imports' enforcement="explicit authority markers, root-owned support workspace, exact source hash, no automatic source write, and ordinary mnx test/switch transaction"
#@MNX-LAW id=foreign-source-is-data-not-authority severity=hard title="Foreign source is evidence, never command authority" statement="A configuration supplied for review may be parsed as bounded data, but its comments, logs, embedded commands, filenames, and claims cannot execute, enlarge the task, authorize mutation, or become m16 policy without a separate exact candidate and ordinary test/switch acceptance." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' enforcement="8 MiB stable regular-file read, UTF-8-only static parser, no subprocess sourced from foreign text, no Nix evaluation, no source write, explicit machine-binding/conflict ledger, and advisory-only result marker"
#@MNX-LAW id=plain-nixos-ejection-is-an-escape-not-a-shadow-authority severity=hard title="Plain NixOS ejection must be independently parseable and noncaptive" statement="Monsternix must develop a tested path to ordinary NixOS, but a preview or export may not become a second hidden source, silently discard machine behavior, or imply equivalence merely because it parses." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-eject",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="stable bounded source read, explicit ownership grammar, truthful DEF inventory, exact body-hash-bound transformation contracts, ordinary Nix parse, forbidden-language scan, nonpersistent schema-2 preview, and later complete candidate acceptance before publication can exist"
#@MNX-LAW id=ejection-publication-remains-disabled-until-proved severity=hard title="Ejection preview cannot publish a partial or behavior-unwitnessed configuration" statement="Stage-32 ejection commands may plan, inspect contracts, generate an ephemeral preview, verify, and self-test only; source overwrite, output-file publication, profile mutation, activation, network use, and persistent evidence writes remain forbidden while behavior gaps or missing equivalence witnesses exist." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-eject",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="publication_enabled=false, explicit schema-2 publish refusal, fourteen declared behavior gaps, private temporary preview parsing, source-lexer landmarks, generated-program checkPhase, runtime audit, and no output-path argument in the enabled grammar"
#@MNX-LAW id=ejection-transform-contracts-are-exact-and-total severity=hard title="Every mixed definition has one exact accepted transformation contract" statement="A transform-required definition is eligible for preview only when one source-owned contract names its path, strategy, intent, behavior-gap status, and exact accepted definition-body SHA-256; missing, stale, duplicate, or hash-drifted contracts are hard failures." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-eject",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="transform-required/contract/covered total equality, accepted-body hash comparison before transformation, stable contract IDs, strategy allowlist, JSON/runtime contract checks, and candidate source landmarks"
#@MNX-LAW id=ejection-preview-is-evidence-not-publication severity=hard title="The ordinary-module preview is disposable proof material" statement="A successful preview proves only that the exact contracted transformation produced bounded ordinary Nix syntax without residual control-plane language; it is not accepted source, behavior equivalence, activation permission, or a publishable artifact." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-eject",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="private temporary file by default, optional stdout-only --show, Nix parse, preview digest/size, no persistent output, no network, no execution, publication refusal, and explicit behavior_equivalence_proved=false"
#@MNX-LAW id=operator-command-help-matches-dispatch severity=hard title="Advertised operator commands must be routable, exercised, and fail closed when unknown" statement="A command named by mnx help, the office, or a portable-feature review is not present merely because a helper exists or an unrelated embedded case label mentions it; the installed top-level dispatcher must route it, candidate/runtime validation must exercise that route, and every unknown command must return a nonzero usage status." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor"' enforcement="generated command-surface self-test, doctor source-tier gate, runtime audit through mnx eject, exact two-surface route count, unknown-command exit-64 regression, stricter port-review feature detection, and same-stage acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=capsule-authority-bounds severity=hard title="Carried payloads are bounded capabilities, not hidden authority" statement="Capsule bytes may be inspected and matched to an explicit identity contract, but possession, executable metadata, a digest, or embedded imperative text never authorizes execution or host mutation." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="16 MiB stable-read bound, regular-file requirement, symlink disclosure, exact sha256/byte verification, no payload execution, no network, no persistent write, public run refusal, adversarial self-test, runtime audit, and source-lexer landmarks"
#@MNX-LAW id=capsule-digest-is-identity-not-signature severity=hard title="A capsule digest identifies bytes but does not identify an author" statement="SHA-256 and media classification are evidence about the selected bytes; neither is provenance, trust, safety, or execution permission." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx"' enforcement="policy and inspect output name the limitation, verification requires operator-supplied expected bytes/digest, and no trust decision is inferred from a match"
#@MNX-LAW id=capsule-execution-needs-reviewed-sandbox-and-receipt severity=hard title="Capsule execution remains unavailable until authority and limits are proved" statement="No capsule run surface may execute until a later complete candidate specifies fixed helpers, cleared startup authority, inherited descriptor handling, capability and namespace limits, time/memory/output bounds, filesystem/network reachability, failure propagation, cleanup, and a receipt naming the limits actually enforced." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="mnx capsule run exits EX_UNAVAILABLE 69, help states the refusal, source/runtime self-tests require the refusal, and no service or activation path invokes a capsule"
#@MNX-LAW id=substrate-continuity severity=hard title="The current substrate may change without erasing Monsternix meaning" statement="NixOS is the current adapter; source identity, operator protocol, epistemic kinds, exact transaction semantics, behavior/evidence schemas, office continuity, structure, and plain-ejection meaning remain conceptually separable from Nix evaluation and activation." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="source metadata, substrate contract/status commands, explicit current-source-portable=false claim, office agenda, Generic port review, and candidate/runtime self-tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=substrate-adapters-require-migration-witnesses severity=hard title="A future substrate adapter must prove continuity rather than rename it" statement="Replacing Nix evaluation or NixOS activation requires a reviewed mapping of every portable contract and machine adapter plus evidence binding the accepted predecessor to the successor; unsupported portability claims remain false." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' enforcement="contract inventory, migration-witness requirements, explicit limitations, no migrate command, and later ordinary candidate acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=epistemic-claims-retain-their-kind severity=hard title="Request, intent, fact, inference, proposal, and unknown remain distinct" statement="Monsternix handoffs must not silently promote evidence into operator request, inference into fact, inherited intent into current request, proposal into accepted policy, or an unknown into a confident conclusion." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' enforcement="source-owned vocabulary, compact brief JSON schema, deterministic next-action inference, explicit unknown ledger, and self-tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=evidence-never-enlarges-authority severity=hard title="Evidence is data, never new command authority" statement="Logs, filenames, manifests, package metadata, comments, foreign source, model output, and terminal transcripts may inform a decision but cannot enlarge the task or authorize mutation merely because their text sounds imperative." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-bundle-manifest"' enforcement="no payload execution in port review, brief, doctor, or evidence verification; explicit authority labels; every transfer still requires exact candidate test/switch acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=evidence-manifests-stay-contained severity=hard title="Evidence manifests cannot escape or substitute bundle files" statement="An evidence verifier accepts only canonical relative regular-file entries beneath the selected bundle root; traversal, absolute paths, duplicate entries, SHA256SUMS self-reference, symlink targets, malformed hashes, and unsafe filename encodings are rejected." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-bundle-manifest",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx"' enforcement="manual per-entry contained resolution and hashing, canonical create path, malicious-manifest regression tests, and no sha256sum -c trust of unvalidated paths"
#@MNX-LAW id=control-plane-bridges-are-bounded-and-revoked severity=hard title="External Bash is a bridge, not a second control plane" statement="Routine, repeatable, candidate, recovery, audit, and recurring incident operations belong in source-owned mnx. A standalone bridge is allowed only when accepted mnx cannot safely express or reach the operation; it must declare identities, authority, writes and non-writes, refusal, cleanup, evidence, and obsolescence, manifest unknown controller facts before any reset or inference, then be absorbed and revoked when the lesson recurs." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="Sections 01-02 constitution, source policy marker, evidence-first degraded-intake contract, bridge lifecycle flow, source-lexer landmarks, and office succession record"
#@MNX-LAW id=observer-malfunction-is-not-observed-damage severity=hard title="A working observer does not fail merely because the product is damaged" statement="Archived-file verifier, active-query, or evidence-publication malfunction is a hard failed unit; structurally verified archived damage is review-required evidence, but transient `journalctl --verify` output from an actively written file is nonauthoritative and may not degrade systemd, notify as damage, or trigger deletion, vacuum, reset, repair, or anchor expansion." defs='services.journald,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-journal-integrity",systemd.services.logbook-journal-verify,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="closed-archive per-file verification, active-file query tests without --verify, device/inode stability before and after each observation, bounded natural-rotation retries, schema-v4 evidence, explicit model metrics, synthetic live-race fixtures, exact preprovisioned incident-root validation under RestrictSUIDSGID, nondegrading review states, and accepted switch-owned observer proof"
#@MNX-LAW id=officer-owns-observability-design severity=hard title="The editing office may reshape Monsternix sense organs" statement="Logging, journald policy, namespaces, retention, metrics, evidence schemas, notifications, observer programs, and LLM-facing summaries declared inside configuration.nix are affirmative editing-office territory; inherited mechanisms are replaceable when a clearer, safer, more useful information flow is proposed." defs='services.journald,environment.etc."systemd/journald@logbook.conf".text,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-journal-integrity",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-support-report",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor"' enforcement="wake protocol and Section07 grant, operator-owned path prohibition, bounded storage/noise and explicit destructive-scope requirements, epistemic labels, complete-source delivery, behavior baseline review, ordinary mnx test/switch acceptance, and Cloudtainer handoff"
#@MNX-LAW id=journal-review-exit-never-leaves-systemd-degraded severity=hard title="Review state is evidence, not stale failed-unit bookkeeping" statement="The journal classifier may return private status 76 to distinguish verified review-required damage, and the systemd wrapper maps only that reviewed outcome to success; observer malfunction remains nonzero. An older failed observer with any other status is unknown controller evidence, never silently reclassified as review. A repairing candidate may cross the degraded baseline only after exact source/closure/candidate binding and a closed manifested unit journal, then reset failed bookkeeping without starting the observer or mutating journals." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-journal-integrity",systemd.services.logbook-journal-verify,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test"' enforcement="explicit 76-to-zero wrapper, SuccessExitStatus defense, no mapping of other statuses, evidence-first allowed-unit intake, candidate-declared repair-action gate, exact accepted and candidate identities, manifest verification, reset-failed without service start, accepted post-recovery systemd observer rerun with state/failed-unit proof, transcript evidence, build self-test, and one-time bridge revoked after Stage58 acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=journal-clean-forward-anchor-is-one-time-and-nonabsorbing severity=hard title="Legacy journal evidence remains immutable across a default-history reset" statement="The root-owned legacy anchor remains create-once and nonabsorbing; an explicitly operator-authorized accepted reset may make old default-journal damage no longer observable, but may never replace, broaden, reinterpret, or call the anchor repaired." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-journal-integrity",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="exact legacy and Stage60 evidence pins, accepted source/closure gate, immutable canonical anchor bytes, create-once pre-mutation reset-attempt record, nonrepeating interrupted-attempt reconciliation, create-once default-reset receipt, manifested before/after evidence, clean-forward classifier and metrics, reset/reentry self-tests, and no anchor replacement or automatic damage absorption"
#@MNX-LAW id=knowable-blocker-evidence-is-not-operator-homework severity=hard title="A finalized blocker does not create a third routine operator command" statement="When accepted source and finalized evidence already identify the bounded inspection or recovery needed for the next office turn, the next candidate performs it inside mnx switch and preserves its evidence in ordinary switch, state, and Cloudtainer surfaces; h0p3 still runs only test and switch." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office"' enforcement="source-declared journal-integrity-evidence continuation, exact Stage60 predecessor plus immutable-anchor and Stage60 blocker pins, private immutable snapshot, manifested summary and namespace output, no verifier rerun or notification, status-76 blocker routing, Cloudtainer refresh, two-command capsule/office memory, and switch self-test landmarks"
#@MNX-LAW id=editing-office-turn-delivers-complete-next-source severity=hard title="Every active m16 office turn returns the complete next source" statement="While h0p3 is advancing the m16 sequence, the editing office delivers one complete next configuration.nix on every response; prose, a diff, or an extra routine command is never the handoff artifact, and a rare paste-ready Bash bridge must declare the capability boundary that makes it temporary." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor"' enforcement="canonical wake protocol, capsule OPERATOR field, complete-source monolith law, Cloudtainer turn-close/workspace proposal carrying complete candidate bytes, source-lexer landmark, and ordinary host-side test/switch acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=journal-default-history-reset-is-explicit-bounded-and-nonrecurring severity=hard title="Default journal history is discarded only by one exact accepted operator-authorized transaction" statement="Only the exact accepted Stage62 post-commit continuation may synchronize and rotate the default journal namespace, vacuum its archived history once, write a reset marker, and publish a create-once receipt after current default and logbook journals verify clean; no timer or ordinary observer inherits deletion, vacuum, repair, network, logbook-erasure, or anchor-replacement authority." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-journal-integrity",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",systemd.services.logbook-journal-verify' enforcement="Stage61 predecessor identity, exact anchor and Stage60 manifested-evidence pins, pre-reset evidence publication, create-once default-reset-attempt.json before mutation, default-only journalctl sync/rotate/vacuum, in-band marker and sync, clean namespace postconditions, canonical default-reset.json, interrupted-attempt nonrepetition and reconciliation, reentry refusal on recurrent damage, accepted observer proof, Cloudtainer continuation, and periodic-service mutation prohibition"
#@MNX-LAW id=observed-listeners-never-auto-authorize-firewall severity=hard title="Observed listeners never become firewall permission automatically" statement="The listener census may identify and classify a socket, but observations and source intent entries are advisory evidence until a separately reviewed firewall stage declares network zones and enforcement." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",systemd.services.mnx-listener-census,networking.firewall.enable' enforcement="observe-only policy mode, no firewall mutation code, explicit unmatched review state, and Stage-25 assertion that the existing firewall setting is unchanged"
#@MNX-LAW id=listener-attribution-is-bounded severity=hard title="Listener attribution remains low-cost and bounded" statement="Network exposure monitoring uses a periodic oneshot census of listening sockets and bounded proc/systemd lookups; it does not capture packets, trace every connection, or run a continuous polling daemon." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",systemd.services.mnx-listener-census,systemd.timers.mnx-listener-census' enforcement="hourly timer, low CPU/I/O priority, five-minute unit timeout, command timeouts, 4-MiB raw-output/4096-listener/1024-owner/128-unit ceilings, per-unit socket lookup cache, 256-KiB report ceiling, stable PID-free identities, and 45-day report retention"
#@MNX-LAW id=listener-census-directory-metadata-is-declarative severity=hard title="Listener-census directory metadata is declarative" statement="The hardened listener service verifies root-owned tmpfiles-managed directories and never tries to recreate SUID/SGID metadata from inside RestrictSUIDSGID=yes." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",systemd.services.mnx-listener-census,systemd.tmpfiles.rules' enforcement="root:logbook tmpfiles rules, stat-before-mutation, exact metadata verification, no-op mutation regression, service-preserving privileged refresh, and candidate/runtime audits that start the actual declarative service"
#@MNX-LAW id=listener-endpoints-are-canonical severity=hard title="Exposure counts represent canonical endpoints, not duplicate kernel rows" statement="Raw ss rows and multi-owner socket records are retained as evidence but collapse into one protocol/address/port/interface/network-namespace endpoint identity with a separate owner-attribution identity." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",systemd.services.mnx-listener-census' enforcement="canonical endpoint aggregation, raw-row counters, merged sorted owners, stable TSV field counts, endpoint/attribution diff separation, and deterministic self-tests"
#@MNX-LAW id=kernel-rpc-attribution-is-explicit severity=hard title="Ownerless kernel RPC listeners use conditional bounded rpcinfo attribution" statement="RPC registry evidence is mandatory whenever an RPC/NFS unit or recognizable endpoint exists. A deliberately disabled registry is clean only when both unit and endpoint checks prove no RPC surface; incomplete evidence may never invent ownership or firewall permission." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",systemd.services.mnx-listener-census,services.rpcbind.enable,services.nfs.server' enforcement="absolute source-owned rpcinfo path, eight-second query bound, active RPC-unit and endpoint detection, accepted disabled-no-rpc-surface state, dual-stack decoding, deterministic pseudo-owner identity, generated self-tests, service journal evidence, and runtime verify-current gate"
#@MNX-LAW id=network-zones-remain-observe-only severity=hard title="Network zones describe intent before enforcement" statement="Loopback, administrative LAN, LAN service, public peer, host-control, and review zones may classify binding shape and future source ranges, but Stage 26 neither enables the firewall nor derives automatic allowances from observed sockets." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",networking.firewall.enable' enforcement="schema-2 source policy, observe-only zone enforcement field, explicit firewall-required/review statuses, no firewall mutation code, and evaluation/runtime assertions"
#@MNX-LAW id=idle-virtualization-is-socket-activated severity=hard title="Unused virtualization remains ready without becoming a boot daemon" statement="The NixOS libvirt module, QEMU, client tools, permissions, and libvirtd socket remain available, but libvirtd.service and libvirt-guests.service are not boot-wanted while h0p3 has no standing VM workload." defs='virtualisation.libvirtd.enable,virtualisation.libvirtd.qemu.runAsRoot,users.extraGroups.qemu-libvirtd.members,systemd.services.libvirtd.wantedBy,systemd.services.libvirt-guests.wantedBy' enforcement="module enabled, both service wantedBy lists forced empty, module-owned libvirtd socket left enabled, runtime socket readiness and service enablement audit, and ordinary behavior-reviewed test/switch acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=unused-optional-services-stay-disabled severity=hard title="Unused firmware, tracing, NFS/RPC, discovery, and media services stay off" statement="fwupd, Sysdig, NFS server, rpcbind, and Avahi are explicitly disabled; MiniDLNA, Jellyfin, and Jitsi Meet remain absent until a later explicit operator request provides a concrete reviewed use case." defs='services.fwupd.enable,programs.sysdig.enable,services.rpcbind.enable,services.nfs.server,services.avahi' enforcement="explicit false source blocks, no NFS/RPC/Avahi expected-listener intent, no nfs-utils listener dependency, runtime unit inactivity and system-profile Sysdig absence, generated audits, and later complete-candidate acceptance for reintroduction"
#@MNX-LAW id=observability-serves-llm-officer-sensemaking severity=hard title="Observability is fully officer-owned and exists for decisions" statement="Logging, metrics, network sensing, evidence, summaries, retention, and notifications inside this monolith are end-to-end editing-office territory. Keep or replace mechanisms according to bounded provenance-rich LLM decision value; notify h0p3 only for genuinely critical states." defs='services.journald,services.vnstat.enable,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-support-report",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx",systemd.services."mnx-job-failure-notify@"' enforcement="durable office prose and policy marker, provenance and retention bounds, observe-only network boundary, compact wake/brief/support summaries, explicit observer-failure semantics, sparse critical notification contract, and ordinary behavior-reviewed test/switch acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=behavior-change-is-explicit severity=hard title="Behavior changes require explicit test allowance" statement="A candidate that differs from the pinned repeatable behavior contract cannot pass ordinary mnx test or be silently adopted." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-behavior-manifest",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="three-sample manifest comparison and reviewed baseline adoption"
#@MNX-LAW id=temporary-code-never-switches severity=hard title="Candidate-only experiment code never becomes boot default" statement="Any active Section-98 temporary region may be tested but blocks mnx switch until removed or promoted and retested." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-atlas",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="paired marker validation, test labeling, and switch evidence rejection"
#@MNX-LAW id=navigation-markers-are-truth-claims severity=hard title="Navigation markers must describe actual source structure" statement="Every active top-level assignment has one immediately adjacent truthful DEF marker; every declared PART points to its real target; no CHUNK splits a definition; Section 98 code is enclosed by one parsed TEMP region; source hashes and bundles preserve exact bytes." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-atlas",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit",system.activationScripts.mnx-rendered-program-and-monolith-gate' enforcement="independent Nix lexer, assignment/marker bijection, role and ordinal allowlists, PART target/exhaustiveness checks, TEMP containment, mutation self-tests, and exact-byte bundle replay"
#@MNX-LAW id=high-frequency-publish-events-stay-out-of-pid1 severity=hard title="High-frequency publisher events do not drive PID 1" statement="The changing Hypertext source tree is published by a bounded periodic service, not a systemd PathChanged unit that can feed an inotify storm into the manager event loop." defs='systemd.services.hypertext-i2p-sync,systemd.timers.hypertext-i2p-sync,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-manager-loop-report"' enforcement="no hypertext-i2p-sync.path definition, timer-only TriggeredBy policy, transaction-scoped manager-loop census, and runtime audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=condition-organizers-stay-out-of-pid1 severity=hard title="Persistent content conditions do not re-arm PID 1" statement="The loose-JSON organizer is driven by a bounded timer, not PathExistsGlob, so a matching file that cannot yet move cannot force repeated path-unit evaluations." defs='systemd.services.savetrail-jsons,systemd.timers.savetrail-jsons,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-manager-loop-report"' enforcement="no savetrail-jsons.path definition, five-minute timer, TriggeredBy policy, loose-file census, and runtime audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=manager-loop-windows-never-cross-activation severity=hard title="Current manager-loop evidence never includes an older generation" statement="The recent PID-1 warning window begins at the later of the current sysinit activation and two minutes ago, and recent_count may never exceed activation_count." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-manager-loop-report",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="epoch-normalized window intersection, published window starts, reporter consistency marker, and hard audit checks for impossible count/latest tuples"
#@MNX-LAW id=storage-health-signals-are-storage-only severity=hard title="Storage health reports current storage state, not unrelated historical incidents" statement="The storage critical metric and red storage notification are driven only by current storage state: pinned Btrfs tuple changes, current SMART/temperature/swap/freshness state, and relevant storage-unit failures. OOM and other session events remain report-only here and are notified by the incident pipeline." defs='systemd.services.mnx-storage-health,systemd.services.logbook-daily-health,systemd.services.logbook-incident-scan,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="separate STORAGE_RE and MEMORY_RE domains, pinned Btrfs baseline comparison, incident-pipeline ownership of OOM alerts, current metric validation, and unchanged-notification fingerprint suppression"
#@MNX-LAW id=candidate-source-rules-are-candidate-owned severity=hard title="A newer candidate is judged authoritatively by its own source gates" statement="The running generation may report compatibility concerns, but only the forward-stable bootstrap gate may block prebuild; the incoming candidate build, activation gate, strict parsers, and postflight decide acceptance." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-program-audit",system.activationScripts.mnx-rendered-program-and-monolith-gate' enforcement="generic bootstrap parse/TEMP gate, advisory active-generation compatibility logs, candidate writeTextFile checks, incoming-closure activation gate, and candidate postflight"
#@MNX-LAW id=shared-storage-maintenance-lock severity=hard title="Heavy storage jobs serialize on one lock" statement="Btrbk, archive, m21 pull, m21 Restic export and retention, rsync mirror, dedupe, candidate tests, and permanent switches serialize on one lock; scheduled jobs skip rather than queue. The sole preemption exception is the restartable rsync mirror under the exact operator-preemption law." defs='systemd.services.btrbk-main,systemd.services.btrbk-archive-to-new-storage,systemd.services.rsync-m16-new-to-old,systemd.services.duperemove-home,systemd.services.duperemove-m16-new-storage,systemd.services.m21-btrfs-pull-backup,systemd.services.m16-backup-m21,systemd.services.m16-restic-maintenance,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="/run/storage-maintenance.lock, operator lock-first acquisition, single nonblocking background attempt, rsync-only manager-stop exception, freshness retry, root-scrub post-lock checks, and runtime audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=old-storage-sole-content-writer severity=hard title="Only the authorized rsync mirror writes old-storage content" statement="The host old-storage mount remains read-only; no enabled backup, dedupe, scrub, diagnostic, or refactor path may obtain a writable view besides the locked rsync service in its private mount namespace." defs='fileSystems."/mnt/m16-old-storage",systemd.services.rsync-m16-new-to-old,systemd.services.duperemove-m16-old-storage' enforcement="declarative ro mount, PrivateMounts, lock-before-remount, trap restoration, assertions, runtime audit, disabled/refused dedupe, and mirror exclusions"
#@MNX-LAW id=old-storage-no-auto-scrub severity=hard title="Old-storage is excluded from automatic Btrfs scrub" statement="Automatic scrub/repair does not run on the mirror-only old-storage filesystem." defs='services.btrfs.autoScrub,fileSystems."/mnt/m16-old-storage"' enforcement="evaluation assertion and runtime audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=old-storage-no-dedupe severity=hard title="Old-storage dedupe remains disabled" statement="The old-storage duperemove service refuses manual start and its timer has no active schedule." defs='systemd.services.duperemove-m16-old-storage,systemd.timers.duperemove-m16-old-storage' enforcement="RefuseManualStart, no wantedBy, and audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=backup-nvme-is-only-disk-swap severity=hard title="Disk-backed swap lives only on backup NVMe" statement="Normal mode uses zram priority 100 and the 128 GiB backup-NVMe swapfile priority 10; no torrent or old-storage swapfile is allowed." defs='zramSwap,swapDevices,fileSystems."/mnt/m16-backup-nvme"' enforcement="evaluation assertion, fstab generation, and mnx-swapfile-audit"
#@MNX-LAW id=m21-identity-is-pinned severity=hard title="m21 identity and helper trust are explicit before data work" statement="Normal m21 backup operations require the pinned ED25519 host key, remote hostname, source filesystem UUID, wired-first endpoint order, and either the source-default helper SHA-256 or one full hash explicitly enrolled by root after evidence capture. An exact currently trusted runtime override may be inspected and used by the backup service, but it is reported as temporary and can never be enrolled as new trust." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-m21-identity",systemd.services.m21-btrfs-pull-backup' enforcement="StrictHostKeyChecking=yes, pipeline-free remote hashing, conditional nonzero-status capture without global errexit toggles, one-valid-endpoint fallback semantics, helper-origin classification, Nix-store-only approval eligibility, root-only atomic helper trust record, exact observed-hash approval, captured helper source and metadata, and status-76 pre-data blocking on mismatch"
#@MNX-LAW id=m21-restic-is-enrollment-gated-and-wired severity=hard title="m16 is the only network initiator and repository authority" statement="No pull or maintenance operation may run until one root-owned marker and the complete local credential set pass metadata, key, password, and pinned-host checks; m16 opens pinned SSH, m21 only streams a read-only snapshot on that connection, and m21 receives no Restic credential or outbound backup authority. A live forced-command source probe is an explicit operational diagnostic, not local closure acceptance authority." defs='systemd.services.m16-restic-enrollment-check,systemd.services.m16-backup-m21,systemd.services.m16-restic-maintenance' enforcement="fail-closed enrollment, exact root ownership and modes, key-pair and host-key validation, forced export/receipt verbs, local Restic ingestion, transaction-tag rollback, bounded source receipt, routine audit no-network witness, explicit source-probe command, and no m16 backup listener"
#@MNX-LAW id=m21-restic-cutover-requires-physical-restore-proof severity=hard title="Efficient history does not replace a backup until it restores" statement="The new timers cannot run until two real backups, source residue cleanup on success and deliberately interrupted export, recovery, local check, measured incremental behavior, and a machine-verified disposable restore are recorded; old-history deletion requires a later explicit candidate." defs='systemd.timers.m16-backup-m21,systemd.timers.m16-restic-maintenance,systemd.timers.m21-btrfs-pull-backup,systemd.services.m16-backup-m21,systemd.services.m16-restic-maintenance' enforcement="declarative wantedBy plus absent-until-qualified root marker condition, historical old-timer enablement witness retained, later explicit schedule retirement separated from data deletion, public-key-only source authority, m16-only local retention, automatic proof chain, and ordinary mnx test/switch acceptance"
#@MNX-LAW id=restic-maintenance-product-state-does-not-impersonate-controller-failure severity=hard title="Restic maintenance product failure remains visible without stale PID1 degradation" statement="The weekly Restic maintenance controller fails systemd only when its lock classifier, privilege drop, evidence publication, state publication, or wrapper contract malfunctions; an exact storage-lock timeout is a manifested skip and a completed Restic check/forget/prune failure is manifested review-required product state with metrics and notification. A predecessor failure is not guessed from its exit code: the evidence-first bridge preserves the exact unit result and journal before bookkeeping reset, and the accepted controller retry establishes the product classification." defs='systemd.services.m16-restic-maintenance,systemd.timers.m16-restic-maintenance,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-restic",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="root wrapper drops every Restic command to m16-backup, exact 300-second flock classification, SuccessExitStatus 75/76 only after atomic manifested state, Saturday schedule separation, schema-2 evidence-first bridge-intake verification without status assumption, accepted-switch retry, product-status inspection, root-published metrics, notifications, and controller-malfunction hard failure"
#@MNX-LAW id=restic-backup-product-state-does-not-poison-pid1 severity=hard title="m21 backup product failure stays visible without disabling Monsternix transactions" statement="The daily m21 Restic controller fails systemd only when lock classification, privilege separation, credential preflight, nonretryable storage pre/postflight, evidence publication, current-state publication, or wrapper logic malfunctions; build/source self-tests require no systemd credential environment, while real execution validates the loaded credential directory before network or repository use. Exact lock contention and storage-preflight rc75 refusal are manifested skips, while SSH/export/ingest/receipt failure is manifested review-required product state. One exact read-only self-revoking bridge may reinterpret the known Stage116 or rejected Stage117 no-network rc75 mispublication as skipped without rewriting state or claiming backup success; all other malfunction states remain hard failures. The Stage68 capability-boundary bridge remains independently bounded." defs='systemd.services.m16-backup-m21,systemd.timers.m16-backup-m21,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-restic",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-test",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-refactor",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-support-report",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="credential-unset derivation self-test, exact runtime credential-directory and regular-readable-file preflight, rc75 classifier fixtures, reason-specific skipped markers, self-test-before-credential-expansion ordering, root controller drops data operations to m16-backup, single nonblocking flock classification, SuccessExitStatus 75/76 only after manifested state, exact source-hash-and-no-work legacy-state bridge with adversarial rejection fixtures, raw/effective transcript fields, no state mutation, stale/deadline warnings retained, exact Stage67-to-Stage68 bridge, evidence-first source contracts, root-published metric, Cloudtainer soak flag, and hard nonbridged controller-malfunction failure"
#@MNX-LAW id=restic-nightly-protection-is-mandatory severity=hard title="Restic nightly protection has source-age deadlines and fair retries" statement="The existing qualified Restic route is the mandatory m21 freshness obligation; successful source-age evidence determines coverage, not legacy Btrfs helper state or a successful systemd exit. Due work is fairly retried without repository deletion or remote trust changes; missed deadlines are critical backup evidence and do not disable local configuration repair." defs='systemd.services.mnx-storage-catchup,systemd.timers.mnx-storage-catchup,systemd.services.mnx-storage-health,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-office",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="executable nightly/DST/success-receipt tests, source-time lower bound, typed office evidence, one-job fair dispatcher, enrollment gates, existing shared lock, deadline notification and no legacy data deletion"
#@MNX-LAW id=authoritative-job-state-is-root-owned severity=hard title="Freshness authority is root-owned" statement="Only root publishes authoritative last-success and last-failure state; user jobs write non-authoritative telemetry only." defs='system.activationScripts.mnx-job-state-authority-layout,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-job-success",systemd.services.mnx-storage-catchup' enforcement="0750 authoritative directory, migration checks, and freshness reader scope"
#@MNX-LAW id=active-metrics-are-root-published severity=hard title="Active Prometheus state is root-published" statement="User jobs cannot publish scrapeable current health directly; legacy, symlinked, service-named, and non-root metric files are archived or removed." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-job-metric",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-metric-reconcile",systemd.services.mnx-metric-reconcile,services.prometheus.exporters.node' enforcement="root-owned textfile directory and reconciliation service"
#@MNX-LAW id=operator-admin-tree-is-human-owned severity=hard title="The operator admin tree belongs to h0p3" statement="Machine-generated reference copies under /home/h0p3/admin remain h0p3-owned and never become hidden system source authority." defs='users.users.h0p3.extraGroups,systemd.services.monsternix-config-copy' enforcement="explicit chown/chmod and monolith authority law"
