#@MNX-FLOW id=mnxcrypt-rootless-vault-session kind=security title="Explicit gocryptfs vault creation and tracked plaintext command session to normal last-session close" source="operator-selected empty/new cipher directory or initialized gocryptfs cipher directory plus source-owned pinentry-qt password after PID-confirmed Presslog pause" destination="verified encrypted backing store, rootless plaintext mount, transient systemd-user FOOBAR cgroups, then syncfs-backed ordinary fusermount3 close" defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnxcrypt-pinentry",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnxcrypt",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/presslog",environment.systemPackages' programs="mnxcrypt,mnxcrypt-pinentry,presslog" lock="per-user per-vault flock plus shared/exclusive vault lease plus exclusive Monsternix secret-prompt lease" state="operator-selected encrypted vault, plaintext mount only while open, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/mnxcrypt lifecycle records, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/monsternix/monsternix-secret-prompt.lock" notes="Create is terminal-only so gocryptfs prints the one-time recovery key directly; the adapter requires anonymous-pipe secret output, passes only an allowlisted environment, PID-confirms Presslog paused before GETPIN, blocks resume through dialog close, and never auto-resumes."
#@MNX-LAW id=mnxcrypt-password-and-lifecycle-boundaries severity=hard title="mnxcrypt create/open credentials and last-session close remain explicit" statement="mnxcrypt may create or open only an explicit rootless gocryptfs vault; create requires an interactive terminal for direct recovery-key display, open requires an explicit command, passwords never enter argv, environment, files, rofi text, or logs, and every source-owned password dialog first PID-confirms Presslog paused, holds an exclusive runtime lease that blocks resume, and leaves capture paused after close; tracked command trees use transient user-service cgroups, and managed close syncs before ordinary unmount and never force- or lazy-unmounts." defs='environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnxcrypt-pinentry",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnxcrypt",environment.etc."monsternix/bin/presslog",environment.systemPackages' enforcement="rendered syntax/checkPhase, anonymous-pipe output guard, child-environment allowlist, O_NOFOLLOW owner-and-mode-checked exclusive prompt flock, hidden PID-bound pause command, no-auto-resume, mocked terminal-create and explicit-command tests, no-passfile/no-sudo/static token gates, live closure projections, exact mount identity, cgroup lifetime, syncfs, normal fusermount3 only, and one post-acceptance real-vault qualification"
#@MNX-LAW id=operator-kept-desktop-surfaces-remain severity=hard title="Automatic desktop readiness and operator-owned post-i3 rollout remain explicit boundaries" statement="Automatic login to h0p3's i3 session, Kodi, Flatpak, Podman, devmon, and udisks2 remain enabled; configuration.nix must not infer, rewrite, or migrate the hand-tuned operator-owned user-space script chain that runs after i3 starts." defs='services.displayManager.autoLogin.enable,services.displayManager.autoLogin.user,services.displayManager.defaultSession,services.xserver.windowManager.i3.enable,services.xserver.desktopManager.kodi,services.flatpak.enable,virtualisation.podman.enable,services.devmon.enable,services.udisks2.enable,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-source-lexer"' enforcement="source policy markers, exact assignment landmarks, candidate source lexer, runtime desktop audit, and ordinary complete-source acceptance before any later migration proposal"
#@MNX-LAW id=network-sensing-serves-future-isolation severity=hard title="Traffic and listener history remain sensory evidence for later isolation and firewall review" statement="vnStat and the bounded listener/exposure ledger remain available to LLM officers so future service binding, namespace isolation, and firewall policy can be based on longitudinal evidence; observations remain advisory and never auto-authorize a firewall rule." defs='services.vnstat.enable,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-exposure",systemd.services.mnx-listener-census,systemd.timers.mnx-listener-census' enforcement="source-declared observe-only zones, bounded hourly census, 45-day ledger, explicit network sensory policy, no firewall mutation, and later separately reviewed enforcement stage"
#@MNX-FLOW id=monsterdesk-private-visual-domain kind=desktop title="Source-owned private nested X11 workstation to bounded LLM desktop control" source="h0p3 X11 session plus reviewed Sandcodex design evidence" destination="private Xephyr displays, network-disabled proof capsules and one dedicated Nicotine pasta/Bubblewrap service" defs='environment.systemPackages' programs="monsterdesk" lock="per-instance user daemon flock, birth-pinned applications and sealed cutover lock" state="/run/user/1000/monsterdesk,/run/user/1000/monsterdesk-nicotine,/home/h0p3/.local/state/monsterdesk,/home/h0p3/.local/state/monsterdesk-nicotine" notes="Stage110 keeps MCP/Openbox proof profiles network-disabled while a separate non-MCP Nicotine instance receives only TCP 2234, four read-only shares, one writable download directory and private copied state; candidate-active mnx test records and quiesces the exact launch tree, proves port release, and restores the exact-package direct fallback before success; sealed switch continuation commits the persistent cutover."
#@MNX-LAW id=monsterdesk-does-not-donate-host-desktop severity=hard title="LLM desktop control remains inside the private visual domain" statement="Monsterdesk application capsules receive only the authenticated nested X socket, private nonactivating D-Bus, private home, explicit read-only audit shares and Nix-store runtime; they never receive the host X socket, host session bus, host home, SSH agent, arbitrary host process control, clipboard, audio or drag/drop bridge." defs='environment.systemPackages' enforcement="empty-root Bubblewrap command, private Xephyr proxy and Xauthority, private D-Bus configuration without service directories, SO_PEERCRED control socket, birth-pinned launch IDs, bounded MCP tools, build self-test and candidate-active hidden live acceptance inside mnx test"
#@MNX-LAW id=monsterdesk-public-peer-cutover-is-profile-specific severity=hard title="A public peer grant belongs only to the reviewed application profile" statement="Ordinary Monsterdesk terminal, audit, preflight and MCP launch profiles remain network-disabled. Only the dedicated Nicotine instance may launch nicotine-live, and that profile receives pasta TCP 2234 bound to the accepted enp4s0 IPv4 address, no UDP ingress, no host-loopback or gateway mapping, four exact read-only shares, one exact writable download directory and private copied state. No profile name or MCP request may generalize that grant." defs='environment.systemPackages,networking.firewall.enable' enforcement="instance-gated internal profile, ordinary CLI/MCP enum exclusion, exact pasta --tcp-ports 192.168.100.100/2234 command identity with --interface/--outbound-if4 enp4s0 and --udp-ports/--tcp-ns/--udp-ns none, active exact-address host-to-namespace connect, Bubblewrap without host home/session bus/X socket, exact bind list, live mountinfo and private-home identity proof, source-owned launcher, exact-package direct rollback fallback, package self-test, real rollback rehearsal and sealed post-acceptance receipt"
#@MNX-LAW id=monsterdesk-live-acceptance-is-mnx-owned severity=hard title="Monsterdesk runtime proof belongs to the canonical candidate transaction" statement="When the source declares the Monsterdesk live acceptance plan, candidate-active mnx-config-audit test runs one hidden ephemeral h0p3 desktop plus one local-only pasta fixture; it proves terminal/authentication/cascade/close, sanitized network-disabled Nicotine GUI, distinct network namespace, explicit loopback TCP forwarding, denial of an unforwarded host-loopback service, bounded UPnP listing, read-only NAT-PMP capability, current listener-port socket classification and exact unexecuted cutover-plan identity, then cleans without touching the main instance or live Nicotine process." defs='environment.systemPackages,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-config-audit"' enforcement="test-mode-only root audit dispatcher, runuser fixed identity, unique runtime/state/viewer, stable O_NOFOLLOW config read, Stage107 hash/port/share/process/wrapper binding, pasta splice-only random-port fixture with -T/-U none and no host/gateway mapping, raw router output withheld and hashed, NAT-PMP opcode-zero response source/format validation with addresses withheld, local listener-port tuples only, synthetic mapping packet fixtures, no external reachability probe, sanitized --unshare-net GUI, confirmed close, cleanup in finally, machine-readable officer evidence and ordinary mnx test rollback"
#@MNX-LAW id=qbittorrent-cutover-is-rollback-tested-and-sealed severity=hard title="qBittorrent moves only through a reversible proof and sealed receipt-last commit" statement="Stage117 candidate-active mnx test proved the exact private qBittorrent TCP/UDP1429 and loopback-only WebUI1234 runtime, two writable payload roots, private state, managed GUI, full launch-tree quiescence, reusable host ports and exact-package legacy restoration. Stage118 records that proof but explicitly defers commitment: family-facing availability now outranks cutover progress, so no candidate or post-acceptance path may stop a healthy client. A later stage may commit only after a parallel replacement is already proven and the final port handoff has an availability witness." defs='environment.systemPackages,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch"' enforcement="standing P2P authority, direct-successor lineage, candidate rehearsal evidence, dedicated qBittorrent instance and user unit, exact source config semantics, bounded archive copy, private config 0600, interface-bound TCP/UDP1429, loopback-only WebUI1234, two exact writable roots, distinct network and mount namespaces, private X11 and D-Bus, receipt-aware accepted-state audit, post-commit action allowlist, receipt-last ordering and exact legacy rollback"
#@MNX-LAW id=nicotine-cutover-is-rollback-tested-and-sealed severity=hard title="Nicotine moves only through a reversible proof and sealed commit" statement="Stage110 candidate-active mnx test may briefly stop the birth-pinned legacy Nicotine client under the standing P2P mandate, copy and harden its current private state, run the real credential-bearing client in the reviewed pasta/Bubblewrap boundary, prove a managed GUI, the configured guest TCP-2234 listener from the isolated network namespace or exact application marker, an exact-address pasta command and active host forward, an outbound Soulseek server connection from namespace state or exact application marker, and namespace separation, close it, and restore the exact Nix-selected direct client before success. Only the exact switched and office-sealed candidate may repeat the transaction into persistent private state and replace the normal launcher; it must prove the prior persistent instance fully stopped before replacing private state, show and re-verify the same birth-pinned isolated launch, and write the receipt only as the last commit point. Accepted-state audits validate immutable semantics before repairing only mode 0600 or UPnP false, restart only after content repair, and re-prove the isolated runtime. Any failed commit removes its receipt, stops the isolated instance and restores the direct legacy fallback." defs='environment.systemPackages,environment.etc."monsternix/bin/mnx-switch",networking.firewall.enable' enforcement="exact PID/start-tick/state stop with zombies never counted alive, zombie-excluding Nicotine inventory and parent-owned child reaping, canonical tuple-to-absolute-Path share normalization and exact bind-spec regression, stable semantic config/share/port checks with current retry-safe byte identity, archive-preserving reflink-auto private copy with cross-filesystem byte-copy fallback and equal bounded inventories, 0600 UPnP-disabled config, immutable-before-mutation hardening evide